Let me set the world registration: world P(px,py,z)=((px-248.5)/100,(355-py)/100,z) on card 497x710. But the figure texture maps into card region via u_card = u*0.83+0.04, v_card = v*0.83+0.117. In figure pixel terms (1049x1500): u = px_fig/1049, v = py_fig/1500.

So card px = 497*(u*0.83+0.04) = 497*(0.83*px_fig/1049 + 0.04)
card py = 710*(v*0.83+0.117) = 710*(0.83*py_fig/1500 + 0.117)

Let me compute: 497*0.83/1049 = 412.51/1049 = 0.39324. 497*0.04 = 19.88.
710*0.83/1500 = 589.3/1500 = 0.392867. 710*0.117 = 83.07.

So:
card_px = 0.39324*fig_x + 19.88
card_py = 0.392867*fig_y + 83.07

And world x = (card_px-248.5)/100, world y = (355-card_py)/100.

So world_x = (0.39324*fig_x + 19.88 - 248.5)/100 = (0.39324*fig_x - 228.62)/100
world_y = (355 - 0.392867*fig_y - 83.07)/100 = (271.93 - 0.392867*fig_y)/100

