For a bone b with parent p: the desired world rotation R_world(b). The pose local rotation Q_local = R_rest_local_world^-1 ... 

Blender formula: `pose_bone.matrix` (armature space) = `parent_pose.matrix @ (parent_rest.matrix_local.inverted() @ bone.matrix_local) @ pose_local_matrix`... The exact relation: 
`pb.matrix = pb.parent.matrix @ (pb.parent.bone.matrix_local.inverted() @ pb.bone.matrix_local) @ pb.matrix_basis`
So given a desired `pb.matrix`, `pb.matrix_basis = (parent_rest_local^-1 @ bone_local)^-1 @ parent_pose^-1 @ desired`. Blender's setter does exactly this. So just use the setter — it's simpler. Cost: need `view_layer.update()` after each set for the children to be correct.

