Implementation of `shell()`:

```python
def shell(mb, rect_px, n, dome, thick, mask, weights_fn, mat, zsign=-1.0):
    x0,y0,x1,y1 = rect_px
    nx, ny = n
    def pos(i,j,front=True):
        u = i/(nx-1.0); v = j/(ny-1.0)
        fxp = x0+(x1-x0)*u; fyp = y0+(y1-y0)*v
        p = fig_to_world(fxp, fyp, 0.0)
        # dome profile: 0 at the border, 1 in the middle
        b = math.sin(math.pi*u)**0.6 * math.sin(math.pi*v)**0.6
        z = dome[0] + dome[1]*b if front else dome[0] - thick
        return Vector((p.x, p.y, z))
    # build front grid, back grid, and rim
```
Masking: for cells where the mask is False, skip creating quads (but vertices may still exist — some unused verts are fine, though they'd get zero weight... they still exist in the mesh with weights, harmless but wasteful; and a fully unused vertex is fine).

