Vertices: front[i][j], back[i][j]. Faces: front quads (winding so the normal faces -z), back quads (normal +z), and rim quads around the border.

Winding matters for Unity backface culling. The front normal should point toward -Z (toward the camera). For a grid with i→+x and j→+y, a quad (i,j),(i+1,j),(i+1,j+1),(i,j+1) has normal +z. So for the front (wanting -z) use the reverse order. For the back, use the normal +z order.

