## Delivered (all inside `Model/**`, nothing else touched)

**`Model/Editor/LadyLakeModelBuilder.cs`** (436 lines, Unity 2019.4, editor-only, **not executed** by me) — exposes `public static LegacyGwent.LadyLakePremium.Editor.LadyLakeModelBuilder.Build()`. It configures the FBX importer (Generic rig, `optimizeGameObjects=false`, `resampleCurves=false`), sets import settings **only on the worker-local texture copies**, builds 4 materials, copies the cycle into `Intro.anim`/`Loop.anim`, builds the `Intro → Loop` AnimatorController, adds the `Animator` to the `FigureRig` root, creates `GripSocket` bone-parented on `HandR` (position derived from the manifest, not hardcoded), ensures the `Grip` marker, saves `Model/FigureRig.prefab`, and writes `unity-build-report.json`.

**`Model/Source/build_figure.py`** — the reproducible authoring source (run headless with Blender 5.1; regenerates every artifact below in ~72 s).

**`Model/Generated/FigureRig.fbx`** (1.72 MB) — 57-bone rig, explicit ≤4-influence weights, bind pose = the approved v5 painting pose. Body 2062 v / 3840 tri (torso ring-loft with bust, shaped head + elven ears, 2 arms, 2 legs), **hands with closed palm shells, 4 fingers × 3 phalanges and a 3-segment inner thumb per hand**, sword 262 v / 480 tri (thickness, fuller, quillons, wrapped grip, faceted pommel), hair 19820 v / 38306 tri as **masked, domed, relief-displaced closed shells with real thickness** + volumetric locks, plus a separate domed face plate.

**Verified, not asserted:** the build re-imports its own FBX and measures it → `fbx_raw_position_used_by_unity [0.9, 1.92, -0.34] == expected_contract_position [0.9, 1.92, -0.34]`, max error `1e-06`, `pass: true`. Sword anchors resolve to grip `1.315,-1.88,-0.15`, guard `1.155,-1.74,-0.14`, tip `-1.415,0.47,-0.12`, pommel `1.715,-2.28,-0.16`. No appearance offset applied.

**Hilt never slides:** the sword is the master; the right arm is solved onto the grip each frame by analytic two-bone IK + a directly set `HandR` matrix, and the sword transform is baked per frame from the evaluated hand with LINEAR keys across the whole closed-grip window.

**`Model/model-report.md`** — full method, contract evidence, and an honest limitations section: face projection wraps at extreme side angles, hair is a shaped shell (contract-permitted) not fibre sim, blade is slim at 512 px, arm ~9 % longer than the painting to satisfy the catch height, and the v5 relaxed hand vs. true-hilt-grip reconciliation.

